      ],
      "observed": "REG2 pin 1 (OUT) is on the +3.3V net, while the +3V3 net contains MCU-related pins but no regulator output. FCC1 and NAVC1 VDD pins appear only in unconnected-(...) nets, and NAVC1 VSS pins are isolated on Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18) rather than connected to GND.",
      "expected": "The 3.3 V LDO output/3V3 rail should feed FCC1 and NAVC1 VDD pins, and MCU VSS/VSSA pins should be connected to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"91\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both microcontrollers are unpowered and NAVC1 lacks a ground reference, so the board cannot boot or perform its intended navigation/flight-control functions.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": [
        "NAVC1",
        "R40",
        "R48",
        "R50"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "R40.1",
        "R48.1",
        "R50.1"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "GPIO_A_NAVC",
        "UART2_TX_NAVC",
        "I2C2_SCL_NAVC"
      ],
      "observed": "The NAVC-side inter-MCU link nets terminate only at series resistors or test points and do not connect to NAVC1. For example, UART2_TX_NAVC contains only R48 pin 1, I2C2_SCL_NAVC contains only R50 pin 1, and GPIO_A_NAVC contains only R40 pin 1.",
      "expected": "The specification states that NAVC and FCC are connected by UART2, I2C, and GPIO links, so these nets should connect to the corresponding NAVC1 pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "NAVC↔FCC run UART2 + I2C + GPIO between the two MCUs"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"143\") (name \"UART2_TX_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"R48\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"40\") (name \"I2C2_SCL_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"R50\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"12\") (name \"GPIO_A_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"R40\") (pin \"1\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Flight Control Computer cannot receive the navigation solution or communicate with the Navigation Computer over the intended UART/I2C/GPIO link.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": [
        "FCC1",
        "UART3_FCC1"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "FCC1.48",
        "FCC1.73",
        "UART3_FCC1.3",
        "UART3_FCC1.4"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "UART3_TX_FCC",
        "UART3_RX_FCC"
      ],
      "observed": "FCC1 VCAP pins are connected to the UART3 connector signals: FCC1 pin 48 (VCAP) is on UART3_TX_FCC with UART3_FCC1 pin 3, and FCC1 pin 73 (VCAP) is on UART3_RX_FCC with UART3_FCC1 pin 4. No VCAP decoupling capacitors to ground are present on these nets.",
      "expected": "STM32H7 VCAP pins are internal regulator output decoupling nodes and must be connected to ground through the required decoupling capacitors, not to UART data lines.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"48\") (name \"VCAP\") (type \"power_out\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"146\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") ... (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") ... (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"4\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU core-supply decoupling nodes are shorted/merged with UART signals, which can prevent the H7 from operating correctly and may damage the regulator or UART lines.",
      "confidence": 0.93
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: the netlist shows the 3.3 V MCU power/ground connections are absent, the NAVC-side inter-MCU link nets are not connected to NAVC1, and FCC1 VCAP pins are merged with UART3 signals, contradicting both the specification and basic MCU design practice."
}

